{
  "summary": "Adds `btck_witness_stack_get_items` to the C libbitcoinkernel API along with a `WitnessStackApi::GetItems` C++ wrapper method. The function performs a single O(n) traversal of a serialized witness stack, populating caller-provided arrays with pointers to each item's data and its byte size. This allows callers to inspect or copy all items in any order without repeatedly scanning the serialized stack.",
  "problem": "Under the serialized witness stack format introduced in #36895, item lookup requires parsing the serialization from the beginning, making random access O(n) in item index. Consumers attempting to retrieve all elements of a witness stack via `btck_witness_stack_get_item_at` suffer O(n^2) runtime.",
  "evidence": [
   "PR description: \"Reading a whole witness stack with btck_witness_stack_get_item_at is O(n^2) because each call walks the items before the one it returns. This function gets every item in one O(n) pass and the caller can read them in any order.\""
  ],
